"""Real Wiley Group cost-basis data — copy this file to wiley_group_private.py
(gitignored, never committed to this public repo) and fill in verified
numbers from the client's actual TD Direct Investing statement.

Source of truth: each monthly statement's "Holdings in your account" table
already gives DRIP-adjusted Quantity + total Book Cost per ticker directly —
no need to reconstruct from individual buy/sell/reinvestment lines. Do NOT
use any file literally named "Trade Blotter" in the client folder as the
source — those have consistently turned out to be pre-trade drafts/estimates
("final share quantities must be calculated at time of trade"), not the
executed fill. Use Clients/DJ/Investment Account Statements/*.pdf instead.

Update this whenever a real trade executes (verified against the new
statement) — this is static config, not re-derived automatically each run.

purchase_date is the ORIGINAL trade-execution date (from the statement's
"Activity in your account" Buy entries, not the "Holdings" section's price
date) — used by trade_blotter.limit_price_full_exit()'s "since purchase"
lookback window. Distinct from as_of, the statement date shares/book_cost
were last verified against.
"""

